    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">MATERIA EXCUSATIONUM</l>
    <l n="2">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="3">1. Qui potestatem habet excusatur.</l>
    <l n="4">2. Non qui post suscepta tutelam bon-</l>
    <l n="5">ris factus est particeps.</l>
    <l n="6">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="7">1. Debitor vel creditor pupilli nequit e-</l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>tutor.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">2. <i>Moribus secus est.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">§. 5.</l>
    <l n="11">1. <i>Tria onera tutelae excusant.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">2. <i>Plures causae imperfectae non excusan[t]</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">§. 6.</l>
    <l n="14">1. <i>Paupertas excusat, &amp; quis paupertim[?]</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">2. <i>Moribus secus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">§. 7.</l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Excusat adversa valetudo.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">§. 8</l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Quid sit literas nescire?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">§. 9. 11.</l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Inimicitiae capitales excusant.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">§. 12.</l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Excusatur cui à patre pupilli mota fu-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>status controversia.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">§. 13.</l>
    <l n="26">1. <i>Grandior aetas excusat.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">2. <i>Minor excusatione non eget.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">§. 14.</l>
    <l n="29">1. <i>Miles non potest esse tutor, sicuti ne-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="30">
      <i>clericus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="31">2. <i>Moribus secus est.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="32">§. 15.</l>
    <l n="33">1. <i>Artes liberales praebent excusationem.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="34">2. <i>Ignavi &amp; desides non excusantur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="35">§. 16.</l>
    <l n="36">1. <i>Tempus excusationis proponitur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="37">2. <i>Modus explicatur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="38">3. <i>Moribus quid obtineat?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="39">de parte patrimonium exeusatur.</l>
    <l n="40" para="true">§. 18.</l>
    <l n="41" para="true">Qui tutelam administravit non tene-</l>
    <l n="42">tur subire ejusdem adolescentis curam.</l>
    <l n="43" para="true">§. 19.</l>
    <l n="44" para="true">1. Maritus non recte uxori datur curator.</l>
    <l n="45" para="true">2. Jure Mosaico uxor subest marito.</l>
    <l n="46" para="true">3. Moribus est omnino in curâ mariti.</l>
    <l n="47" para="true">§. 20.</l>
    <l n="48" para="true">Sententia ex falsâ causâ pro tutore</l>
    <l n="49">lata, est ipso jure nulla.</l>
    <l n="50" type="heading" level="1" caput="26" para="true">LIBR. I. TIT. 26.</l>
    <l n="51" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Susp. Tutor.</l>
    <l n="52" type="heading" level="2" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="53" para="true">SUspecti actio abusive dicitur crimen.</l>
    <l n="54" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="55" para="true">1. Quinam removeans suspectos?</l>
    <l n="56" para="true">2. An suspecti cognitio possit demandari?</l>
    <l n="57" para="true">3. Moribus quid obtineat?</l>
    <l n="58" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="59" para="true">1. Omnis tutor suspecti postulatur.</l>
    <l n="60" para="true">2. Non tamen parens.</l>
    <l n="61" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="62" para="true">1. Suspecti postulatio est quasi publica.</l>
    <l n="63" para="true">2. Mulieres postulant suspecti.</l>
    <l n="64" para="true">§ 4.</l>
    <l n="65" para="true">1. Minores, non tamen impuberes suspe-</l>
    <l n="66">cti, quem postulare possunt.</l>
    <l n="67" para="true">2. Quid moribus obtineat?</l>
    <l n="68" para="true">§. 5.</l>
    <l n="69" para="true">1. Definitur suspectus.</l>
    <l n="70" para="true">2. Definitur quasi suspectus.</l>
    <l n="71" para="true">§. 6.</l>
    <l n="72" para="true">1. Suspectus ob dolum remotus, est infamis.</l>
    <l n="73" para="true">2. Licet sententia infamia non memine-</l>
    <l n="74">rit.</l>
    <l n="75" para="true">§. 17.</l>
    <l n="76" para="true">Tutor personae, non rei datur &amp; nec</l>
